Authentication in action
In this section, we will see how to implement authentication and make our web pages
restricted for unauthenticated requests.
To achieve authentication, we should adopt some sort of mechanism that provides us with
a way to authenticate a user. In general cases, if a user is logged in, that means they are
already authenticated.
In our web application, we will also follow the same approach and make sure that the user
is logged in before accessing the restricted pages, views, and operations:
