The IObserver<T> interface has the OnComplete, OnError, and OnNext methods that we
have to implement in the ProductReporter class. The purpose of the OnComplete
method is to notify the subscriber that the job has been done and then flush out the code.
Furthermore, OnError is invoked when an error occurs during execution, while OnNext
provides information of the next element in the sequence of a stream.
